pplicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHII NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKYO ELECTRON LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKAHORI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKIAGE, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHII, NOBUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKYO ELECTRON LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>AKAHORI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKIAGE NORIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHII NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKAHORI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKIAGE, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHII, NOBUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A vacuum chamber (2) is provided with a gas supply unit (51) surrounding a region confronting a wafer (10) for blowing out a processing gas toward the wafer (10).  The vacuum chamber (2) is intermittently fed with microwaves for creating a plasma from a high-frequency power generating unit (6) by turning on/off the generation at a frequency of 30 Hz to 500 Hz.  As a result, the residual gas over the wafer (10) is replaced by new processing gas while the microwaves are off.  Thus, no substantial difference in the degree of gas dissociation between the central portion and the peripheral edge portion of the wafer (10) arises, thereby conducting a uniform plasma processing.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Une enceinte à vide (2) est équipée d'une unité d'alimentation en gaz (51) entourant une région qui fait face à une plaquette (10) de manière à souffler un gaz de traitement en direction de la plaquette (10). Cette enceinte à vide (2) est alimentée par intermittence avec des micro-ondes, aux fins de génération d'un plasma, à partir d'un générateur haute fréquence (6) alternativement activé et désactivé à une fréquence comprise entre 30 et 500 Hz. De ce fait, le gaz résiduel à la surface de la plaquette (10) est remplacé par du gaz de traitement neuf lorsque les micro-ondes sont arrêtées. Il ne se produit ainsi aucune différence sensible dans le degré de dissociation du gaz entre la partie centrale et la partie périphérique de la plaquette (10), ce qui permet de mettre en oeuvre un traitement au plasma uniforme.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>